# Keep every checked-out file byte-identical to what is committed.
#
# This repository ships SHA-256 manifests that pin the exact bytes of sibling
# files. Any line-ending translation performed during checkout changes those
# bytes and makes every recorded hash fail to verify.
#
# `-text` alone is not enough: with core.autocrlf=true, git still normalises
# text files on the way into the object store. `-text -crlf` disables both the
# checkout conversion and the commit-side CRLF normalisation, so the blob always
# holds the file's literal bytes.
#
# Applied per extension rather than as `*`, because `* -text` does not cover the
# commit-side normalisation on every git version.
*.py       -text -crlf
*.json     -text -crlf
*.jsonl    -text -crlf
*.csv      -text -crlf
*.txt      -text -crlf
*.md       -text -crlf
*.log      -text -crlf
*.cfg      -text -crlf
*.toml     -text -crlf
*.bin      -text -crlf
*.npz      -text -crlf
*.parquet  -text -crlf
*.docx     -text -crlf
# The last rule also covers the extension-less members under large_files/
# (`sources.jsonl.part/part00`, ...), which are raw byte ranges of JSONL and
# Parquet files and must be concatenated back verbatim. Their SHA-256 is checked
# by restore_large_files.py, so a single translated byte would abort the restore.
*          -text -crlf
